nks beside the held NYPL illustration, tied to seven reviewed native picture comparisons. Sauganash gains four taller lower-front windows and a narrower entrance leaf with a case, transom and sidelights. Sources and reconstruction bounds are recorded as liberties.\n\nThis is incremental progress on T-2386 and T-2383; both original tickets remain open. The Sauganash MASTER/WEB are regenerated, with the other 24 default models and their WEB files unchanged. Three existing Carpenter comparisons are genuinely refreshed and directly reviewed for the changed hotel context; Carpenter’s model, cameras and source pictures are unchanged.\n\nThe catalogue measures 548 sources, 224,868 raw bytes and 59,470 gzip bytes (native level 6). Its raw ceiling is 228,000 bytes and the wire ceiling remains 120,000. Form-note keys follow the existing READ policy without changing residents or population assignments.\n\nValidation: all four local source-check parts passed on authored feature head 1855273d. On final integration head `0e838b35b5ba32b61ccd01499310520e160ab4a2`, the native 53-step dependency tail settles after two passes; focused native checks, Fort/Pullman fixtures, all three PR preflight questions and the published-file contract pass. Fresh published desktop (1280×800) and phone (390×780) checks pass with default geometry release enabled, zero page/console/network/server errors and all six captures directly reviewed. Native published stage 3 passes 107/107 checks at each viewport with zero failures/page errors. Source, publication and Git metadata guards remain unchanged. GitHub’s required gate must pass on this unchanged head before merge.\n\n[Final screenshots, native transcripts and complete recovery](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/121eaee6e28f74696131cfd71850e26c8cc259b1/evidence/wolf-sauganash-2026-11-03/0e838b35b5ba-final-default-visitor/RECOVERY.md). [All four authored source-check transcripts](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/21aa2718167d440dcd5073f2d1672caa7a77929e/evidence/wolf-sauganash-2026-11-03/pushed-1855273/RECOVERY.md).\n\nLimits: Wolf’s diagnostic comparisons do not claim a calibrated historical viewpoint or accepted street-arrival framing; the normal arrival currently foregrounds Miller House. The unresolved 1935 poster remains inspection-only. Sauganash’s contextual Carpenter views do not sign off the whole hotel. Door traversal, the entire 15-part runtime suite and full original-ticket closure are not claimed. No follow-up ticket is created.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-02T22:16:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T04:03:42Z","closed_at":"2026-11-03T04:03:42Z","merged_at":"2026-11-03T04:03:42Z","merge_commit_sha":"18c037e9f756a5190787ef1bd77bacce78331ad1","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/wolf-point-reviewed-views-20261102","ref":"steward/wolf-point-reviewed-views-20261102","repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events"